## Endpoint resolution & active config
- The request body type is `OwnerFieldsDto`; the response is `OwnerDto`.
- Active Spring profile: `spring.profiles.active=h2,spring-data-jpa` (`src/main/resources/application.properties:20`), so the live repository is the Spring Data JPA proxy `SpringDataOwnerRepository`, NOT `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` (`@Profile("jpa")`) or the JDBC impl.
- Security is OFF by default: `petclinic.security.enable=false` (`application.properties:49`) activates `DisableSecurityConfig` (`.anyRequest().permitAll()`). The `@PreAuthorize` on the handler is only enforced when the other config (`BasicAuthenticationConfig`, gated on `enable=true`, which has `@EnableMethodSecurity`) is active. See section 8.

---

## 1. The @RestController method (POST /api/owners)

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class-level (lines 75-78): `@RestController @CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders="errors, content-type") @RequestMapping("/api")`, `implements OwnersApi`.

The POST mapping itself lives on the generated interface `OwnersApi` (`target/generated-sources/openapi/.../rest/api/OwnersApi.java`), which is `@Validated` (line 44). Method `addOwner` (lines 79-87): `@RequestMapping(method=POST, value="/owners", produces/consumes application/json)`, parameter `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. Combined with the class `/api` → **POST /api/owners**. So `@Valid` triggers Bean Validation on the DTO before the controller body runs.

The concrete handler, `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (lines 142-186), verbatim body:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    String idempotencyKey = this.request.getHeader("Idempotency-Key");
    if (idempotencyKey != null && !idempotencyKey.isBlank()) {
        Integer existingId = this.idempotentCreates.get(idempotencyKey);
        if (existingId != null) {
            Owner existing = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(existingId);
            if (existing != null) {
                return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(existing), HttpStatus.OK);
            }
        }
    }
    normalizeAddress(ownerFieldsDto);
    validateRequiredFields(ownerFieldsDto);
    validatePostcode(ownerFieldsDto);
    normalizeTelephone(ownerFieldsDto);
    normalizeEmail(ownerFieldsDto);
    rejectDuplicateIdentity(ownerFieldsDto);
    rejectDuplicateHousehold(ownerFieldsDto);
    rejectCityAtCapacity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity());
    rejectFutureRegistrationDate(ownerFieldsDto);
    defaultRegistrationDate(ownerFieldsDto);
    rejectDailyLimit(ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate());
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    assignCustomerCode(owner);
    assignHouseholdId(owner);
    assignHouseholdMemberCount(owner);
    assignNamesakeCount(owner);
    assignMembershipNumber(owner);
    assignBulkSignupWarning(owner);
    assignPossibleDuplicate(owner, Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    if (idempotencyKey != null && !idempotencyKey.isBlank()) {
        this.idempotentCreates.put(idempotencyKey, owner.getId());
    }
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), owner.getMembershipLevel(),
        owner.getMembershipNumber());
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Note: there is also a **v2** controller `OwnerRestControllerV2` (`.../rest/controller/v2/`) but it only exposes `GET` listing (`listOwnersPage`); it does NOT handle create.

## Precise execution order (create path)
0. **Bean Validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` (from `@Valid`) — runs before the method.
1. Idempotency-Key short-circuit (returns 200 with the original owner if the key was seen).
2. `normalizeAddress` — composes/normalizes address lines (upper-case, collapse whitespace, expand ST/RD/AVE), writes back `address`.
3. `validateRequiredFields` — firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone non-blank → else `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400).
4. `validatePostcode` — if present, region range check → `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).
5. `normalizeTelephone` — to E.164, writes back; invalid → `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400).
6. `normalizeEmail` — if present, syntax + disposable-domain check, lower-cases, writes back → `InvalidEmailException` (400).
7. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` — whole identityKey (`tel|email|householdId`) vs existing non-deleted owners → `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).
8. `rejectDuplicateHousehold` — unless `sharesHousehold=true`, householdId collision → `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).
9. `rejectCityAtCapacity` — ≥50 owners in city → `CityAtCapacityException` (409).
10. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` — supplied date after today → `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).
11. `defaultRegistrationDate` — defaults to today if null, then rolls weekend/holiday forward to next business day; writes back.
12. `rejectDailyLimit` — ≥100 owners on that business day → `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429).
13. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` — MapStruct maps DTO→entity (id & pets ignored).
14. Derived-field assignment (all pre-persist, in-controller): `assignCustomerCode` (SHA-256 of tel+lastName, region prefix, de-duped), `assignHouseholdId` (SHA-256 lastName|postcode), `assignHouseholdMemberCount`, `assignNamesakeCount`, `assignMembershipNumber`, `assignBulkSignupWarning` (>80/day), `assignPossibleDuplicate`.
15. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — persists.
16. Idempotency map update; AUDIT log line; map to `OwnerDto`; set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`; return **201 CREATED**.

Note many of the derived-field/uniqueness helpers call `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (full table scan) each time — several separate full scans per create.

