## 6. Side-effects (all in the controller, before/around persist)
- Mutates the request DTO in place: address normalization, telephone→E.164, email lower-casing, registrationDate defaulting + business-day roll.
- Sets entity-derived fields: `customerCode`, `householdId`, `householdMemberCount`, `namesakeCount`, `membershipNumber`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`.
- Idempotency: in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String,Integer> idempotentCreates` keyed on `Idempotency-Key` header (`OwnerRestControllerV1:103`, populated at 176-178).
- Audit logging: dedicated SLF4J logger named `"AUDIT"` emits an info line after save (179-181).
- No emails/notifications, no event publishing (`ApplicationEventPublisher` not used), no password encoding on this path. `Owner` also exposes many `@Transient` read-only derived getters (salutation, fiscalYear, membershipPoints/Level, contactPreference, ageBand, checkDigit, telephoneDisplay, identityKey, selfLink) that `OwnerMapper` invokes when building the response `OwnerDto` — these are read-time only, not persisted.
- Mapping: `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct, `uses=PetMapper`). `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`; `toOwnerDto(Owner)` fills the transient/derived fields (incl. `locality`/`timezone` via `LocalityLookup`).

## 7. Exception handlers (@ControllerAdvice)

`src/main/java/.../rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` (`@ControllerAdvice`). Relevant to create:
- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 with `errors` + `schemaValidationErrors` (Bean Validation failures) — lines 152-188.
- `RequiredFieldsMissingException` → 400 (199-210).
- `InvalidEmailException` → 400 (230-241); `InvalidPostcodeException` → 400 (252-263); `FutureRegistrationDateException` → 400 (402-413).
- `DuplicateIdentityException` → 409 (297-308); `DuplicateHouseholdException` → 409 (334-346); `CityAtCapacityException` → 409 (358-369). (`DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateEmailException` handlers exist at 274-321 but the current create path throws the consolidated `DuplicateIdentityException` instead.)
- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` → 429 (380-391).
- `AccessDeniedException` re-thrown so Security handles 401/403 (103-106); catch-all `Exception` → 500 (115-122); `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404 (132-143).
All responses are RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` with `timestamp`, `errors`, and `schemaValidationErrors` properties. Exception classes live in `.../rest/controller/*Exception.java`.

## 8. Spring Security affecting this endpoint
- Handler annotated `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` → requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (`security/Roles.java:8`).
- `security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java` — `@ConditionalOnProperty("petclinic.security.enable"="true")`, has `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled=true)`, `.anyRequest().authenticated()`, HTTP Basic, JDBC auth, BCrypt encoder. Only when active is `@PreAuthorize` actually enforced.
- `security/DisableSecurityConfig.java` — `@ConditionalOnProperty(...="false")`, `.anyRequest().permitAll()`.
- Because `application.properties:49` sets `petclinic.security.enable=false`, the **default runtime has security disabled**: `DisableSecurityConfig` is active, `@EnableMethodSecurity` is absent, so the `@PreAuthorize` is not enforced and POST /api/owners is open. Enabling the flag switches to authenticated + role-checked.
